  "notes": "{抱|だ}く means to hold someone or something in one's arms, typically embracing warmly.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Passive: {抱|だ}かれる (to be held/embraced)\n\nPRONUNCIATION:\n- {抱|だ}く: to physically hold/embrace (common, spoken)\n- ⟦{抱|いだ}く→抱く：02010_idaku⟧: to harbor feelings, to hold in one's heart (literary)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{抱|だ}いて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates the ongoing state of holding something: ⟦{子供|こども}→子供：00554_kodomo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|だ}いて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ (is holding a child).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{子供|こども}→子供：00554_kodomo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|だ}く: to hold a child\n- ⟦{強|つよ}く→強い：00820_tsuyoi⟧{抱|だ}く: to embrace tightly\n- ⟦{優|やさ}しく→優しい：02640_yasashii⟧{抱|だ}く: to hold gently\n- ⟦{枕|まくら}→枕：03898_makura⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|だ}いて⟦{寝|ね}る→寝る：00470_neru⟧: to sleep hugging a pillow\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{抱|だ}きしめる→抱きしめる：06044_dakishimeru⟧: to hug tightly\n- ⟦{抱|だ}っこ→抱っこ：09091_dakko⟧: being held (child's word)",
